---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Architecture Overview">
  <p>
    ArrowCrab is an interactive viewer for directed acyclic graphs (DAGs).
    It draws computation graphs on an HTML5 canvas with automatic layout,
    orthogonal edge routing, and pan/zoom/expand/collapse.
  </p>

  <h2>Design Goals</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Zero dependencies.</strong> Everything is built on the
      Canvas 2D API with vanilla TypeScript. No UI framework.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Structural correctness.</strong> Nodes and edges share a single integer
      grid, so edges can never cross through nodes. This is guaranteed by the grid
      structure, not by collision checks.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Compound graphs.</strong> Nodes can contain subgraphs that expand
      and collapse inline. Layout goes bottom-up so parent nodes size themselves
      around their children.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Causal cones.</strong> Click a node to highlight all its ancestors
      and descendants. Everything else dims so you can focus on the relevant
      data flow.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tech Stack</h2>
